---
import Body from '../layouts/Body/Body.astro';

import TextScroller from '../components/TextScroller/index.astro';
import HorizontalProgress from '../components/HorizontalProgress/index.astro';
import ExperienceTimeline from '../components/ExperienceTimeline/index.astro';
import Job from '../components/ExperienceTimeline/Job.astro';

import { RAMP } from '../three/palette';

// low, mid and high elevation
const progressColors = [RAMP[2], RAMP[4], RAMP[6]];
---

<Body title="Projekt Neu | Harry Whorlow">
  <div class="theme" data-theme="dark">
    <section id="first-section" class="first-section relative h-screen w-full overflow-hidden">
      <canvas id="moon-canvas" class="block h-full w-full" />

      <div class="pointer-events-none absolute top-0 left-0 p-8 md:p-12">
        <h1 class="text-[10rem] leading-none font-bold">I'm Harry,</h1>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base">I build tools, teams, and occasionally climb stuff.</p>
      </div>

      <HorizontalProgress colors={progressColors} />
    </section>

    <section id="second-section" class="flex min-h-screen flex-col">
      <TextScroller />

      <div class="p-10">
        <h1 class="mt-10 text-[10rem] leading-none font-bold">Open Source</h1>

        <p class="mt-4 w-200 text-base">
          I've been contributing to open source for two years now, with commits across the ecosystem and encounters with
          developers all over the globe.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-4 w-200 text-base">
          Most of that time has been spent with TanStack. On 07/03/25, after a few months of implementing features,
          fixing bugs and documenting APIs,{' '}
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/corbincrutchley/" target="_blank" class="text-high underline">
            Corbin Crutchley
          </a>{' '}
          messaged me to check my email. There, with an almost holy glow, was the subject line:{' '}
          <span class="bg-low box-decoration-clone px-1 text-black">
            @crutchcorn has invited you to join the @TanStack organization
          </span>
          . Since then, it's given me opportunities I'm fortunate to have and friendships I'll be forever thankful for.
        </p>

        <p class="mt-4 w-200 text-base">
          On its face, open source is a strange thing: people giving up their free time so faceless mega corporations™
          can profit from their labour. But there's something to it, something about programming in the dead of night on
          features a developer somewhere in the world will use. You'll probably never meet them, but for a moment,
          you're building something together.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="third-section" class="flex flex-col">
      <ExperienceTimeline colors={[RAMP[2], RAMP[4], RAMP[6]]}>
        <Job company="AllMyHomes" dates="01/05/22 - 17/07/22">
          <p>
            I think about AllMyHomes more than you'd expect for a three-month role. I was fresh out of a bootcamp and
            asked to migrate the micro-frontends I was responsible for into a monolith repository. When my senior,{' '}
            <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/lukasz-milik/" target="_blank" class="text-high underline">
              Łukasz
            </a>
            , said to "just copy over the APIs," I did, I copied thirteen thousand lines verbatim. When he said he'd
            speak to my skip-level manager after taking one look at the PR, I was certain I was finished. What happened
            instead was training and a second chance. I'm not the greatest developer in the world, but I'm a competent
            one now, and I owe much of that to Łukasz.
          </p>

          <p>
            Unfortunately my time at AllMyHomes was cut short, as the summer of 22 drew to a close, and governments
            around the world were increasing interest rates to fight inflation, the funding was cut. Three rounds of
            layoffs later the company no longer exists.
          </p>
        </Job>

        <Job company="Technoly" dates="01/09/22 - PRESENT">
          <p>
            Technoly is where I really progressed as a developer. I was given the freedom to make mistakes and had very
            little oversight for the majority of my time here. Decisions I made years ago as a junior developer
            frequently show up again in tasks I have today. I feel that oftentimes we learn the most as developers when
            we are confronted with decisions we made in the past, a lesson that many developers are robbed of if their
            time at a company is on the shorter side.
          </p>

          <p>
            I have learnt a lot here: I have become confident in my developer skills, deepened my understanding of
            advanced TypeScript, and even became a maintainer of TanStack... an organisation I once revered as a junior
            developer, and still do.
          </p>
        </Job>

        <Job company="TO BE CONTINUED..." dates="PRESENT - FUTURE">
          <p>My story is still developing, lets see where I go next.</p>
        </Job>
      </ExperienceTimeline>
    </section>

    <section id="forth-section" class="flex min-h-screen flex-col">
      <div class="p-10">
        <h1 class="mt-10 text-[5rem] leading-none font-bold">So Lets work,</h1>
        <h1 class="text-[10rem] leading-none font-bold">TOGETHER</h1>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <style>
    .theme {
      --theme-bg: #000;
      --theme-fg: var(--main-text-light);

      background-color: var(--theme-bg);
      color: var(--theme-fg);
      transition:
        background-color 0.6s ease,
        color 0.6s ease;
    }

    .theme[data-theme='light'] {
      --theme-bg: var(--grey-light-main);
      --theme-fg: var(--main-text-dark);
    }

    #second-section {
    }
    #third-section {
    }
    #forth-section {
      opacity: 0;
    }
  </style>

  <script>
    import gsap from 'gsap';
    import ScrollTrigger from 'gsap/ScrollTrigger';

    import { createMoon } from '../three/moon';

    gsap.registerPlugin(ScrollTrigger);

    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
      const canvas = document.querySelector<HTMLCanvasElement>('#moon-canvas');
      const moon = canvas && createMoon(canvas);
      const theme = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.theme')!;
      const setTheme = (value: 'dark' | 'light') => (theme.dataset.theme = value);

      // one scrubbed timeline drives the pin, so the copy, the bars and the theme flip can't drift apart
      const intro = gsap.timeline({
        defaults: { ease: 'none' },
        scrollTrigger: {
          trigger: '.first-section',
          start: 'top top',
          end: '+=150%',
          pin: true,
          scrub: true,
          invalidateOnRefresh: true,
          onUpdate: (self) => moon?.setScroll(self.progress),
          // the last bar reaches the right edge exactly as the pin ends
          onLeave: () => setTheme('light'),
          onEnterBack: () => setTheme('dark'),
        },
      });

      // move the hero copy up off-screen in step with the pinned moon animation
      intro.to(
        '.hero-copy',
        {
          y: () => {
            const copy = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.hero-copy');
            return copy ? -(copy.offsetTop + copy.offsetHeight) : 0;
          },
          duration: 1,
        },
        0
      );

      // staggered so the bars arrive one after another, together spanning the whole pin
      intro.to('.progress-bar', { scaleX: 1, duration: 0.8, stagger: 0.1 }, 0);

      // once the experience lines reach the left edge, go back to dark and bring in the next section
      const fourth = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#forth-section')!;
      document.addEventListener('experience:drawn', () => {
        setTheme('dark');
        gsap.to(fourth, { opacity: 1, duration: 0.6, overwrite: true });
      });
      document.addEventListener('experience:undrawn', () => {
        setTheme('light');
        gsap.to(fourth, { opacity: 0, duration: 0.6, overwrite: true });
      });

      gsap.to('#overlay-secondary', {
        opacity: 1,
        scrollTrigger: {
          trigger: '.second-section',
          start: 'top bottom',
          end: 'top center',
          scrub: true,
        },
      });
    });
  </script>
</Body>
